{
  "slug": "aws-dev-toolkit",
  "name": "Aws Dev Toolkit",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code plugin tailored to startups building on AWS. It includes domain specific skills and cross-cutting skills that required for builders and operators.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **35 skills**, **11 agents** and **3 MCP servers**.\n\n- **Skills** (35): `agentcore` (Deep-dive into Amazon Bedrock AgentCore platform design, service selection, deployment, and production operations), `api-gateway` (Design and configure Amazon API Gateway APIs), `aws-architect` (Design and review AWS architectures following Well-Architected Framework principles), `aws-compare` (Compare 2-3 AWS architecture options side-by-side across cost, complexity, performance, security, and operational burden), `aws-debug` (Debug AWS infrastructure issues, deployment failures, and runtime errors), `aws-diagram` (Generate AWS architecture diagrams in Mermaid or ASCII from a description, existing IaC, or conversation context), `aws-health-check` (Quick health check on the current AWS account — security posture, cost waste, reliability gaps, and operational readiness), `aws-plan` (End-to-end AWS architecture planning — discovery, design, security review, cost estimate, and SCP recommendations), and 27 more\n- **Agents** (11): `agentcore-sme` (Amazon Bedrock AgentCore subject matter expert for building production-ready AI agents), `aws-explorer` (Read-only AWS environment explorer), `bedrock-sme` (Amazon Bedrock subject matter expert emphasizing cost-efficient usage patterns), `container-sme` (Container expert for ECS, EKS, and Fargate), `cost-optimizer` (Deep AWS cost optimization expert), `iac-reviewer` (Reviews infrastructure-as-code changes for correctness, security, and best practices), `migration-advisor` (Cloud migration expert), `networking-sme` (AWS networking expert covering VPC design, hybrid connectivity, DNS, CDN, load balancing, and service connectivity), and 3 more\n- **MCP servers** (3): `awsiac`, `awsknowledge`, `awspricing`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install aws-dev-toolkit@claude-community` from `aws-samples/sample-claude-code-plugins-for-startups` (`plugins/aws-dev-toolkit`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
